WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.694
Nvidia halted chip

00:00:01.506 --> 00:00:02.814
shipments to Southeast

00:00:02.626 --> 00:00:03.192
Asia

00:00:03.726 --> 00:00:05.058
Nvidia has told

00:00:04.870 --> 00:00:06.497
its manufacturing partners

00:00:06.309 --> 00:00:07.299
to stop shipping

00:00:07.110 --> 00:00:08.301
servers to four

00:00:08.113 --> 00:00:09.692
south-east Asian countries

00:00:09.835 --> 00:00:10.660
as the US

00:00:10.542 --> 00:00:11.674
steps up export

00:00:11.485 --> 00:00:12.983
controls on AI

00:00:12.818 --> 00:00:14.032
computing power

00:00:14.566 --> 00:00:15.591
Partners such as

00:00:15.403 --> 00:00:17.030
Dell and Supermicro

00:00:17.113 --> 00:00:18.622
which package Nvidia's

00:00:18.434 --> 00:00:19.683
chips into servers

00:00:19.790 --> 00:00:20.686
told buyers in

00:00:20.498 --> 00:00:21.252
Malaysia

00:00:21.417 --> 00:00:22.278
Singapore

00:00:22.384 --> 00:00:24.141
Thailand and Indonesia

00:00:23.965 --> 00:00:24.990
that their orders

00:00:24.802 --> 00:00:25.839
will not ship

00:00:26.366 --> 00:00:27.415
It is unclear

00:00:27.227 --> 00:00:28.158
whether the halt

00:00:28.064 --> 00:00:29.054
is temporary

00:00:29.193 --> 00:00:30.101
The move comes

00:00:29.913 --> 00:00:30.749
as the US

00:00:30.561 --> 00:00:31.587
tries to prevent

00:00:31.399 --> 00:00:32.601
Chinese access to

00:00:32.448 --> 00:00:33.898
AI computing power

00:00:34.146 --> 00:00:35.148
three people with

00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:35.844
knowledge of the

00:00:35.656 --> 00:00:36.492
matter say

00:00:37.014 --> 00:00:38.028
Full story on

00:00:37.839 --> 00:00:38.735
the dashboard
